{"assertions":[{"answerability":"answerable","basis":"Durand's article \"The New Testament\" in the Catholic Encyclopedia (vol. 14, 1912) dates the Johannine corpus as a body: \"The Johannine writings belong to the end of the first century, from the year 90 to 100 (approximately).\"","basis_class":"traditional-catholic","date":"90 A.D. to 100 A.D.","derived":false,"disposition":"disputed","inherited":true,"label":"from the year 90 to 100 (approximately)","note":"The window is asserted of the Johannine writings collectively — the Gospel, the three Epistles and, with a noted exception, the Apocalypse — not of the Fourth Gospel by itself.","precision":"interval","profile":"catholic-traditional-v1","relation":"composition","reporting_exception":null,"scope":"John","sources":["artifact.catholic-encyclopedia.volume-14.new-york-1912.newadvent-14530a-0a19aa2c"],"subject":"composition.gospel-of-john","title":"The Gospel of St John"},{"answerability":"answerable","basis":"Fonck's article \"Gospel of St. John\" in the Catholic Encyclopedia (vol. 8, 1910): \"According to the general opinion, the Gospel is to be referred to the last decade of the first century, or to be still more precise, to 96 or one of the succeeding years.\" The PRECEDING sentence admits that \"As to the date of its composition we possess no certain historical information\".","basis_class":"traditional-catholic","date":"96 A.D. to 100 A.D.","derived":false,"disposition":"disputed","inherited":true,"label":"96 or one of the succeeding years","note":"The same article reaches the same figure by a second route, from the Monarchian Prologue's statement that John wrote the Gospel \"after he had composed the Apocalypse on the Island of Patmos\", which \"would therefore refer the composition of the Gospel to A.D. 96 or one of the years immediately following\" — an argument that puts the Gospel later than the Apocalypse. Recorded as an interval and not as an approximate year: the source prints no \"about\", and both bounds are its own — \"the last decade of the first century\" caps it and \"96 or one of the succeeding years\" opens it. The approximate-year encoding this claim carried until now was rendered to consumers as \"about 96 A.D.\", a hedge the source does not print, and it both admitted years the source excludes (94-95) and excluded years it allows (97-100).","precision":"interval","profile":"catholic-traditional-v1","relation":"composition","reporting_exception":null,"scope":"John","sources":["artifact.catholic-encyclopedia.volume-8.new-york-1910.newadvent-08438a-7620a92c"],"subject":"composition.gospel-of-john","title":"The Gospel of St John"}],"chronology_status":"composition-only","locus":"John.10.14","reason":"","requested_profile":"catholic-comprehensive-v1","resolved_profiles":{"composition":"catholic-traditional-v1"},"status":"ok","v":1}
